{"id": "20470510", "revid": "25112844", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20470510", "title": "Mike Donovan (baseball)", "text": "Michael Beckam Donovan (October 18, 1881 \u2013 February 3, 1938) was a professional baseball player. He played parts of two seasons in Major League Baseball for the Cleveland Naps in 1904 and the New York Highlanders in 1908, primarily as a third baseman. In seven career games, he had five hits and two RBIs, all of them with the Highlanders. He batted and threw right-handed.\nDonovan was born in Brooklyn, New York and died in New York, New York. Donovan was working for Consolidated Edison as a security guard when he was accidentally shot and died, after a co-worker's gun accidentally discharged."}
